Title: Probe reuse of Zotero 6012 inference runtime
Created: 2026-08-30
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-08-30T16:09Z Minh Ha-Duong created

2026-08-31T05:38Z claude note FIRST EXIT CRITERION ANSWERED at source 2026-08-30 (clone of zotero/zotero, PR head 77e2c4b), and the answer is stronger than 'not exposed yet'. No supported external call exists, and none can exist while the runtime is Gecko's. Two findings. (1) Against the true merge-base 3af8cea, the PR touches NO server, API or connector file -- git diff --name-only over the PR range returns nothing under xpcom/server/ -- so the boundary this ticket asks to confirm rather than infer is confirmed, and confirmed at source rather than from internal JavaScript names. (2) The reason is structural: Zotero.ML is a 236-line wrapper (chrome/content/zotero/xpcom/ml.js, absent from main, added by this PR) over Firefox's own runtime -- ChromeUtils.importESModule('resource://gre/actors/MLEngineParent.sys.mjs') at :69, createEngine at :124, ModelHub at :208, EngineProcess at :231, gated on Services.prefs browser.ml.enable / checkForMemory / minimumPhysicalMemory at :92-98; embeddings.js calls Zotero.ML.createEngine with backend 'onnx-native' at :670 and :3785, and takes its tokenizer from chrome://global/content/ml/transformers.js at :1570. resource://gre and chrome://global resolve only inside a Gecko process, and ChromeUtils/Services are XPCOM globals, so a Node process cannot reach any of it. Consuming an existing API is therefore OFF the outcome list for 0491; what remains is the bridge specification or deferral. TWO THINGS FOR THE REMAINING CRITERIA. The comparison criterion has to carry R30 (ratified 2026-08-30): the advantage zoteus holds is that a native process reaches CUDA where that runtime has no GPU path, so a bridge that moves inference into Zotero forfeits the requirement rather than merely trading RAM. And the portable half of this runtime -- transformers.js over onnxruntime -- is what bench/ already runs, and upstream asks for the same native ONNX backend, so the reusable part is already had; what the bridge would buy is model download, cache custody and engine lifecycle, not inference itself
--- body ---
## Context

Zotero PR #6012 already places native ONNX inference in Firefox's separate,
memory-gated inference process. Its internal `Zotero.ML` creates engines and
manages the model cache; `Zotero.Embeddings` owns a curated model registry and
`embedQuery()` / `embedPassages()`. At PR head `77e2c4b`, the changed-file set
contains no local-API route exposing those calls, so direct reuse by an external
zoteus process appears unavailable. Confirm that boundary rather than inferring
an API from internal JavaScript names.

## Scope

Determine whether zoteus can reuse Zotero's #6012 inference process through a
supported bridge, avoiding another loaded model and another system service.
Explore an official Zotero local-API contract first. A private monkey-patch or
mandatory Zotero plugin is evidence about feasibility, not an adoption path.

## Exit criteria

- Verify against the current #6012 head whether any supported external call can
  request query and batched passage embeddings.
- If absent, specify the smallest upstream bridge: model/version identity,
  query versus passage role, batching, dimension, runtime/provider identity,
  cancellation, errors and availability. It accepts text transiently and
  exposes neither Zotero's embedding database nor arbitrary profile access.
- Test whether vectors returned by Zotero's native ONNX backend satisfy X8
  against the same registry entry used in-process; a failure keeps provider in
  vector identity.
- Compare cold-start, steady RAM, model-cache custody, version skew and failure
  behavior with in-process zoteus and a generic local endpoint.
- Record one outcome for ticket 0491: consume an existing API, propose the
  bridge upstream, defer pending #6012, or reject reuse with the blocking fact.
